{title: Dancing Before the Lord}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 18:20–28; 19:11–17; 25:44; 2 Samuel 3:13–16; 6:16–23; 6:23}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Saul's daughter Michal loved David
He [Bb]killed two hundred Philistines
To [C]win her hand from the king
She [Dm]let him escape the night
Through the window he ran away
A household [Bb]idol in the bed
Saul [C]sought his life in vain
But she de[Dm]ceived the messengers
[Bb]She said he was sick and weak
[C]He fled to save his own [F]life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Dancing before [C]the Lord
Leap[Dm]ing with joy in the [Bb]street
Michal looked [F]down from the win[C]dow
And de[Bb]spised him in her heart
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Years passed and David was king
He asked [Bb]for his wife to return
[C]Paltiel followed weeping
Sent [Dm]away to go home
The ark of the covenant came
Into [Bb]the city of David
Da[C]vid leaped and danced before
The [Dm]Lord of hosts on high
[Bb]Michal came out to meet him
With [C]scorn upon her face
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Dancing before the [C]Lord
Leap[Dm]ing with joy in the [Bb]street
Michal looked [F]down from the win[C]dow
And [Bb]despised him in her heart
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
How [Dm]the king has exposed himself
[Bb]Before the eyes of slave girls
Da[C]vid said I will be humbled
In my own [Dm]eyes I am small
Be[Bb]fore the Lord I will celebrate
And be [C]held in honor by them
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Michal [Bb]had no child to the day of her [C]death
She remained [Dm]in childless ways
{end_of_verse}
